    "publisher": "National Library of Medicine (NLM/NIH)",
    "title": "Type 2 Diabetes - Overview",
    "content": "Topic: Type 2 Diabetes\nSection: Overview\nPublisher: National Library of Medicine (NLM/NIH)\n\nType 2 diabetes is a chronic metabolic disease where blood glucose levels are too high. In type 2 diabetes, the body cells do not respond normally to insulin; this is called insulin resistance. The pancreas makes more insulin to try to get cells to respond, but eventually cannot keep up, leading to elevated blood sugar levels. Over time, high blood sugar damages nerves, blood vessels, eyes, kidneys, and the heart.",
    "source_url": "https://medlineplus.gov/diabetestype2.html",
