    "title": "Pneumonia - Overview",
    "content": "Topic: Pneumonia\nSection: Overview\nPublisher: National Library of Medicine (NLM/NIH)\n\nPneumonia is an infection that inflames the air sacs (alveoli) in one or both lungs. The air sacs may fill with fluid or pus (purulent material), causing cough with phlegm, fever, chills, and difficulty breathing. Community-Acquired Pneumonia (CAP) is acquired outside of hospitals. Streptococcus pneumoniae is the most common bacterial pathogen.",
    "source_url": "https://medlineplus.gov/pneumonia.html",
