  {
    "document_id": "mplus_tuberculosis_overview",
    "source_id": "MedlinePlus",
    "source_name": "MedlinePlus Health Topics (NLM / NIH)",
    "publisher": "National Library of Medicine (NLM/NIH)",
    "title": "Tuberculosis (TB) - Overview",
    "content": "Topic: Tuberculosis (TB)\nSection: Overview\nPublisher: National Library of Medicine (NLM/NIH)\n\nTuberculosis (TB) is a contagious infectious disease caused by the bacterium Mycobacterium tuberculosis. TB primarily affects the lungs (pulmonary TB) but can also affect the lymph nodes, brain, kidneys, spine, and joints (extrapulmonary TB). It spreads through airborne droplets when an infected person coughs, sneezes, or speaks.",
    "source_url": "https://medlineplus.gov/tuberculosis.html",
