  {
    "document_id": "mplus_tuberculosis_symptoms",
    "source_id": "MedlinePlus",
    "source_name": "MedlinePlus Health Topics (NLM / NIH)",
    "publisher": "National Library of Medicine (NLM/NIH)",
    "title": "Tuberculosis (TB) - Symptoms",
    "content": "Topic: Tuberculosis (TB)\nSection: Symptoms\nPublisher: National Library of Medicine (NLM/NIH)\n\nSymptoms of active pulmonary TB include persistent cough lasting 2 to 3 weeks or longer, coughing up blood or sputum (hemoptysis), chest pain, unprovoked weight loss, low-grade evening fever, drenching night sweats, fatigue, and loss of appetite.",
